Oikos is proprietary software. The code in this repository — including the panel,
the add-on server, the Home Assistant integration, images and documentation — is
protected by copyright and remains the exclusive property of the author.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   a) Install and use Oikos on YOUR OWN Home Assistant instances, under the terms
      of the subscription (named licence, tied to your email address, valid for a
      single instance; 40-day trial on first run).
   b) Read the code in this repository for study, security review and bug reports.
   c) Create and distribute your own CUSTOM CARDS for Oikos: they are your work,
      and the "oikos-card-starter" SDK is published under the MIT licence for that
      purpose.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO, without the author's written permission
   a) Copy, republish, redistribute or resell Oikos or any part of it, whether
      original or modified, free of charge or for a fee.
   b) Create derivative works of the panel, the server or the integration, or
      publish forks intended for use by third parties.
   c) Decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the parts distributed in compiled
      form, except to the extent such restriction is prohibited by law.
   d) Remove, circumvent or disable the licence check, the subscription limits, or
      any authorship and copyright notice.
   e) Use the "Oikos" name, logo or distinctive signs for unauthorised products,
      services or distributions.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS
   By submitting code, text or translations (pull requests, issues, discussions)
   you grant the author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free licence
   to use, modify and distribute your contribution as part of Oikos. You retain
